# Manual API checks — IntelliJ HTTP client (ADR-0019), committed alongside the endpoints it tests.
# Open in IntelliJ IDEA and click the gutter arrow, or run with the `ijhttp` CLI.
# Add a request block here whenever a route is added, so the endpoint surface is always
# exercisable without a browser or curl incantation.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@webOrigin = http://localhost:3000

### Health — 200 while every dependency is up, 503 once one is not.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/health
Accept: application/json

### Health, as the browser sees it: same request with the web app's Origin, so the response must
### carry Access-Control-Allow-Origin (ADR-0015's allow-list).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/health
Accept: application/json
Origin: {{webOrigin}}

### CORS preflight from an origin that is NOT on the allow-list — must be refused with 403.
OPTIONS {{host}}/api/v1/health
Origin: http://evil.example.com
Access-Control-Request-Method: GET

### Unknown route — must return the standard error envelope, not an HTML/plain-text 404.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/does-not-exist
Accept: application/json
